{
  "dom_id": "step-q29643",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}={x}^{-5}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-5$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4}}{-4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{4}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
